    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d599">

                <pb facs="0783" n="689" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg689"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Taylor.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-10-15"><hi rendition="#italic">October 15,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 589.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s instructions
                    Nos. 568 of the 12th and 576 of the 24th ultimo, 581 of the 2d and 583 of the
                    6th instant, I inclose copies of a letter<anchor n="1" xml:id="d599-f1"/> from
                    Louis Wertheimer and of two dispatches<anchor n="1" xml:id="d599-f2"/> from our
                    consul-general at Habana, relating to Mr. Wertheimer’s claim against the Spanish
                    Government based on the action of the Governor-General of Cuba in refusing to
                    allow the shipment of 307 bales of tobacco purchased before the date of issue of
                    General Weyler’s proclamation.</p>
                <p>You will present this case with the others to the Spanish Government.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
